From: OpenAI <openai@example.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: rtl8231: update reg_mask_xlate to 7.3 gpio-regmap API

Linux 7.3 added an enum gpio_regmap_operation argument to the gpio-regmap
reg_mask_xlate() callback. Update the RTL8231 callback signature to match;
the driver still derives the register from the base address, so the new
operation argument is unused.

Signed-off-by: OpenAI <openai@example.com>

---
 drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-rtl8231.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-rtl8231.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-rtl8231.c
@@ -462,7 +462,8 @@
 /*
  * GPIO controller functionality
  */
-static int rtl8231_gpio_reg_mask_xlate(struct gpio_regmap *gpio, unsigned int base,
+static int rtl8231_gpio_reg_mask_xlate(struct gpio_regmap *gpio,
+	enum gpio_regmap_operation op, unsigned int base,
 	unsigned int offset, unsigned int *reg, unsigned int *mask)
 {
 	unsigned int pin_mask = BIT(offset % RTL8231_BITS_VAL);
